    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Visualize U.S. Crop Data\r\n\r\nUse the imported datasets to create two data visualizations about U.S. crops.\r\n\r\n### Line Chart\r\n\r\nUse `line_chart_data` from `avocado_counts.csv` to create a line chart that:\r\n\r\n- Uses `Year` for the x-axis and `Avocado Yield` for the y-axis\r\n- Includes a meaningful title and axis labels\r\n- Displays when the program runs\r\n\r\n### Bar Chart\r\n\r\nUse `bar_chart_data` from `US_agricultural_crops.csv` to create a bar chart that:\r\n\r\n- Uses `Crop` for the x-axis and `2000 Yield` for the y-axis\r\n- Includes a meaningful title and axis labels\r\n- Displays readable x-axis labels\r\n- Displays when the program runs\r\n\r\nRun the program and check that both charts display the correct data clearly.\r\n\r\n::: details [Not sure where to start?]\r\n\r\nUse AI Tutor to:\r\n\r\n- View examples using different data\r\n- Learn how a Matplotlib function works\r\n- Understand an error message\r\n\r\nThen use what you learn to write your own code.\r\n\r\n:::",
    "ai_tutor_available": "false",
    "submittable": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
